sarah palin former alaska governor and  2008 vice presidential nominee for the  republicans she is running for congress  as we know she's trying to make a  comeback into public life after a long  hiatus and she has now passed the first  hurdle for getting the job this is  actually a special election that's going  on in alaska since don young died  earlier this year after representing the  at-large district in alaska for 49 years  now alaska has this interesting system  where they have all of their candidates  regardless of party appear on the same  ballot for a first round of voting the  top four vote getters then move on to  the next round of voting where ranked  choice voting is used to determine who  comes out on top we just had the first  round of voting and we're still getting  the votes in but as of now the results  show that palin has 29.8 percent of the  vote followed by another republican  named nick begich at 19.3 percent then  we have al gross at 12.5 percent and  democrat mary pelota at seven point five  percent so those should be the four who  advance and move on to the second round  notably not making the cut yet still  getting an impressive 4.5 percent of the  vote was democratic socialist candidate  santa claus which i didn't realize that  santa lived up in alaska i thought he  lived up in canada or like maybe the  international territory that makes up  the north pole but apparently he's an  alaska resident and who knows maybe  he'll get him next time palin's near 30  in the vote is a commanding uh lead  ahead of everyone else but then when you  note that there's something like 50  other candidates you have to think about  how the other voters are going to  coalesce when the  candidate number drops down to four  also you have ranked choice voting so  that makes it a little bit harder to  predict compared to a normal election so  who knows what will happen in the second  round uh you just don't know who people  are going to coalesce around maybe the  other republican will do better in the  second round maybe the independent al  gross will win there's a good chance  that maybe she's not able to pull this  thing off and that would of course be a  major blow to trump's endorsement record  and to the state of trumpism in this  country because not only is palin  endorsed by trump she in a lot of ways  was trump before trump was trump notably  based on how incompetent and  inarticulate she was and we didn't  realize that someone so unqualified  could serve in public office at such a  high level but you know then we got  donald trump and now it's somewhat  normalized also not helping palin and  trump is the fact that alaska politics  are a lot different than the rest of the  country they tend to be more centrist  and they like the more reasonable  candidates more often than not so  who knows if she can pull it off there  it's really just not the reddest state  in the country plus many alaskans view  palin as a quitter because she quit her  job as governor  10 plus years back to do a reality tv  show so that just didn't sit very well  with them how do they know that she's  not going to resign early from her seat  in congress but fear not because palin  has an excellent excuse in her back  pocket in case she doesn't come out on  top she went on mark levin's show a few  weeks ago  and she said that you know if i don't  win uh clearly it's because of voter  fraud yeah she's using that routine  let's take a look at this clip from  about a month ago yeah whether i have a  a good shot or not they're they're i  think about 50 candidates in this race  it's a real bizarre race and there's  ballot  50 and um  mark you'll just really appreciate this  it's mail in only ballots uh no hand  counting to tabulate got to go through a  dominion  computer to count everything and  i like yesterday mark i received four  ballots in the mail i didn't even ask  for any ballots uh one for one of the  daughters who doesn't live here  she has hasn't claimed residency in  alaska since she moved outside  we call anything outside of alaska i'm  trying to say murkowski  well um you know who wrote this bizarre  election plan that we have right now  going on with the ranked choice voting  that's coming up and the mail and only  ballots and all that was lisa  murkowski's attorney  i believe  well yeah i mean do i do i have a shot  at it yeah i i have a shot at it um  it's it's  bizarre though you know  this kind of voting system so i hope the  rest of america keeps track of what's  going on in alaska so it doesn't happen  to them well that's certainly the  trumpian playbook right there if you win  everything was on the up and up and you  just got more votes from the good people  of your district to your state but if  you lose you didn't really lose it was  just rigged and what can you do you were  a victim so that's nice you have that in  your back pocket as an excuse and you  can really use it in any election that  you want to of course i want palin to be  defeated and there's really a good  chance of that happening we'll have to  see it's going to be tight but maybe  this is a race that we can get ourselves  involved in but part of me wonders like  if sarah palin does become a congress  person would that have entertainment  value would she have these wacky off the  rail speeches on the house floor that  would be worth watching i also wonder if  she would  interact well with people like marjorie  taylor green and lauren beaubert would  she be too crazy for them would they be  too crazy for her i just don't know so  you know if she does end up pulling off  the win in this race that will be like  the one saving grace we get to see how  she functions as a member of congress  but hopefully it doesn't get to that and  hopefully sarah palin is defeated when  it's time for the second round of voting  of course there'll be more elections to  come and we'll be following all of them  all right thanks very much to david for